  "research_id": "sec-investor-advisory-committee",
  "title": "SEC Investor Advisory Committee — 2026 meeting record",
  "question": "What did the SEC Investor Advisory Committee actually say and vote in 2025–2026, which official records exist, and how does that advice sit next to the Commission’s tokenized-NMS, transfer-agent, NMS and disclosure clocks?",
  "bluf": "The IAC is a Dodd-Frank §911 advice body, not a rulemaker, but its recommendations and the Commission's public engagement with them are useful policy-development signals. The March 12 tokenization record is the strongest current chain: Peirce tested the draft's exact provisions before the September 17 Commission order carried several similar constraints. The order does not cite the IAC, so this is direct engagement plus substantive convergence, not proven formal uptake. March and September discussions also contemplated a less document-bound, more machine-readable EDGAR architecture, but EBO owns the system answer and the full Commission owns any binding disclosure change. The joined EDGAR signal analysis places those discussions beside the Form N-PORT data-boundary failure, current support contract, OIG workflow findings and FDTA standards; together they support a provisional regulatory-data-plane hypothesis, not a disclosed Commission design. Citation, engagement, convergence, legal effect, system deployment and operating implementation remain separate clocks.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-20T16:20:12-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "Base meeting package verified through September 17. September 18 uptake and EDGAR work adds Commissioner engagement, attribution checks, SEC/OIG/contract/FDTA evidence and controlled architectural inference. The September 20 join adds DERA and Enforcement organization, 24-hour trading, market-data revenue, transformed-data vendor and circuit-breaker objects. IAC captions remain non-verbatim discovery evidence; the order does not cite the IAC; June 4 and September 10 minutes were still not posted when checked.",
  "use_note": "Use the uptake tracker to separate an explicit IAC citation, direct Commissioner or staff engagement, substantive convergence without citation, divergence, an effective legal object, actor-specific operative relief, and observed implementation. Use the EDGAR control map to separate IAC design discussion from Commission rule/form authority, EBO business ownership and OIT deployment. Do not treat a webcast, caption, recommendation, speech, later Commission order or software release as interchangeable authority.",
  "library_state": "current",
